          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The first statement is a special case of the general fact that
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits+of+presheaves+are+computed+objectwise"} limits of presheaves are computed objectwise
            %p
              For the second statement, first assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathbf{X}, \mathbf{Y}]
              does exist. Then by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} hom-adjunction isomorphism
              we have for any other presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Z}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
              of the form
            #eq:InternalHomIsoInPresheaves.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Set
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Z
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Set
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Z
                    %mo ×
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{[\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]}(\mathbf{Z}, [\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y}])
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    Hom_{[\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]}(\mathbf{Z} \times \mathbf{X}, \mathbf{Y})
                    \\,.
            %p
              This holds in particular for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Z
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Z} = y(c)
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable functor
              (i.e. in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+image"} essential image
              of the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              implies that if it exists, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathbf{X}, \mathbf{Y}]
              must have the claimed form:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %msup
                                  %mi 𝒞
                                  %mi op
                                %mo ,
                                %mi Set
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %msup
                                  %mi 𝒞
                                  %mi op
                                %mo ,
                                %mi Set
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    [\mathbf{X}, \mathbf{Y}](c)
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Hom_{[\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]}( y(c), [\mathbf{X}, \mathbf{Y}] )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq Hom_{ [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set] }( y(c) \times \mathbf{X}, \mathbf{Y} )
                    \\,.
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              Hence it remains to show that this formula does make
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:InternalHomIsoInPresheaves"} (1)
              hold generally.
            %p
              For this we use the equivalent definition of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
              in terms of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+counit"} adjunction counit
              providing a system of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+arrows"} universal arrows
            %p
              Define a would-be
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+counit"} adjunction counit
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation"} evaluation
              morphism, by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mi ev
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Y
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %msup
                                  %mi 𝒞
                                  %mi op
                                %mo ,
                                %mi Set
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ev
                                  %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi c
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbf{X} \times [\mathbf{X} , \mathbf{Y}]
                    \&amp;\overset{ev}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{Y}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbf{X}(c) \times Hom_{[\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]}(y(c) \times \mathbf{X}, \mathbf{Y})
                    \&amp;\overset{ev_c}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{Y}(c)
                    \\\
                    (x, \phi) &amp;\mapsto&amp; \phi_c( id_c, x )
                    }
            %p
              Then it remains to show that for every morphism of presheaves of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                        %mi f
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X} \times \mathbf{A} \overset{\phantom{A}f\phantom{A}}{\longrightarrow} \mathbf{Y}
              there is a
              %em unique
              morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo ˜
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde f \;\colon\; \mathbf{A} \longrightarrow [\mathbf{X}, \mathbf{Y}]
              such that
            #eq:UniversalArrowConditionForEvaluationMapInPresheaves.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi A
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi X
                                %mo ×
                                %mover
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ˜
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mi f
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↙
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi ev
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbf{X} \times \mathbf{A}
                    \&amp;&amp; \overset{ \mathbf{X} \times \widetilde f  }{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp;
                    \\mathbf{X} \times [\mathbf{X}, \mathbf{Y}]
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{ \mathrlap{f} }}\searrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\swarrow_{ \mathrlap{  ev } }
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{Y}
                    }
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commutativity
              of this diagram means in components at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \mathcal{C}
              that, that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \mathbf{X}(c)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in \mathbf{A}(c)
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi ev
                              %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi f
                                %mo ˜
                              %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi f
                                %mo ˜
                              %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi c
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    ev_c( x, \widetilde f_c(a) )
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    (\widetilde f_c(a))_c( id_c, x )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; = f_c( x, a )
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              Hence this fixes the component
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo ˜
                      %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde f_c(a)_c
              when its first argument is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+morphism"} identity morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_c
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi d
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \;\colon\; d \to c
              be any morphism and chase
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (id_c, x )
              through the naturality diagram for
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi f
                          %mo ˜
                        %mi c
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde f_c(a)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo ,
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mover
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo ˜
                                  %mi c
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi a
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi g
                                    %mo *
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi g
                                    %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mo ,
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mover
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo ˜
                                  %mi c
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi a
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mi d
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAA
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi id
                              %mi c
                            %mo ,
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi g
                            %mo ,
                            %msup
                              %mi g
                              %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi g
                              %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %msup
                              %mi g
                              %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(c,c) \times \mathbf{X}(c)
                    \&amp;\overset{ (\widetilde f_c(a))_c }{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{Y}(c)
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{ g^\ast }}\big\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\big\downarrow^{\mathrlap{ g^\ast }}
                    \\\
                    Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(d,c) \times \mathbf{X}(d)
                    \&amp;\overset{ (\widetilde f_c(a))_d }{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    \\mathbf{Y}(d)
                    }
                    \\phantom{AAAA}
                    \\array{
                    \\{ (id_c, x ) \} &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \{ f_c( x, a ) \}
                    \\\
                    \\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\{ (g, g^\ast(x)) \}  &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \{ f_d( g^\ast(x), g^\ast(a) ) \}
                    }
            %p
              This shows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo ˜
                      %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\widetilde f_c(a))_d
              is fixed to be given by
            #eq:ComponentFormulaForEvaluationMapInPresheaves.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo ˜
                      %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\widetilde f_c(a))_d( g, x' )
                    \\;=\;
                    f_d( x', g^\ast(a) )
            %p
              at least on those pairs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g,x')
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x'
              is in the image of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^\ast
            %p
              But, finally,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi f
                        %mo ˜
                      %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\widetilde f_c(a))_d
              is also natural in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mover
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo ˜
                                  %mi c
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi g
                                    %mo *
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi g
                                    %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mover
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo ˜
                                  %mi d
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi d
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbf{A}(c)
                    \&amp;\overset{ \widetilde f_c }{\longrightarrow}&amp; [\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y}](c)
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{g^\ast}}\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow^{\mathrlap{g^\ast}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathbf{A}(d)
                    \&amp;\overset{ \widetilde f_d }{\longrightarrow}&amp; [\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y}](d)
                    }
            %p
              which implies that
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ComponentFormulaForEvaluationMapInPresheaves"} (3)
              must hold generally. Hence naturality implies that
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:UniversalArrowConditionForEvaluationMapInPresheaves"} (2)
              indeed has a unique solution.
          %h2#definition_in_terms_of_homs_of_direct_images Definition in terms of homs of direct images
          %p Often another, equivalent, expression is used to express the internal hom of presheaves:
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} pre-site
            with underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            that just means that we have a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_X
            on which we consider
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaves
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msubsup
                      %mi S
                      %mi X
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in PSh(S_X) := [S_X^{op}, Set]
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                to each object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in PSh(X)
                and in particular to each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi X
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in S_X \hookrightarrow PSh(X)
                there is naturally associated the pre-site
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                with underlying category the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comma+category"} comma category
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi U
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_U = (Y/Y(U))
            %li
              %p
                that the canonical
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stuff%2C+structure%2C+property"} forgetful
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi j
                          %mrow
                            %mi U
                            %mo →
                            %mi X
                          %mi t
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi U
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^t_{U \to X} :  S_U \to S_X
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} morphism of pre-sites
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi j
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_{U \to X} : X \to U
                induces the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
                functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi j
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo *
                      %mo :
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (j_{U \to X})_* : PSh(X) \to PSh(U)
                which we write
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo ↦
                        %mi F
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \mapsto F|_U
          %p
            Then in these terms the above
            %strong internal hom
            for presheaves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo :
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  hom : PSh(X)^{op} \times PSh(X) \to PSh(X)
          %p
            is expressed for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F,G \in PSh(X)
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  hom(F,G) = U \mapsto Hom_{PSh(U)}(F|_U, G|_U)
                  \\,.
          %h2#relation_of_the_two_definitions Relation of the two definitions
          %p To see the equivalence of the two definitions, notice
          %ul
            %li
              that by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              we have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_U
              is simply the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+category"} over category
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi U
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_U = S_X/U
            %li
              by the general properties of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors+and+comma+categories"} functors and comma categories
              there is an equivalence
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(S_X/U) \simeq PSh(S_X)/y(U)
            %li
              which identifies the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)|_U : PSh(S_X) \to PSh(S_U)
              with the functor
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 2
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ((-)\times y(U) \stackrel{p_2}{\to} y(U)) : PSh(S_X) \to PSh(S_X)/y(U)
            %li
              and that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mrow
                          %mi PSh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mrow
                          %mi PSh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{PSh(S_X)/y(U)}(y(U) \times F, y(U) \times G) \simeq Hom_{PSh(S_X)}(y(U) \times F, G)
          %h2#presheaves_over_a_monoidal_category Presheaves over a monoidal category
          %p
            It is worth noting that in the case where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is itself a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \otimes, I)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Psh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Psh(X)
            is equipped with another (bi)closed monoidal structure given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            product and its componentwise right adjoints. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be two presheaves over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \star G
            can be defined by the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
            formula:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\star G = U \mapsto \int^{U_1,U_2\in X} Hom_X(U, U_1\otimes U_2) \times F(U_1) \times G(U_2)
          %p Then we can define two right adjoints
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi F
                  %mo \
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mo −
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi G
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F\star - \dashv F \backslash -
                  \\qquad -\star G \dashv - / G
          %p
            by the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} end
            formulas:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo \
                  %mi H
                  %mo =
                  %mi V
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \backslash H = V \mapsto \int_{U\in X} F(U) \to H(U\otimes V)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H / G = U \mapsto \int_{V\in X} G(V) \to H(U\otimes V)
          %p
            In the case where the monoidal structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is cartesian, the induced closed monoidal structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Psh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Psh(X)
            coincides with the cartesian closed structure described in the previous sections.
          %h2#closed_monoidal_structure_on_sheaves Closed monoidal structure on sheaves
          %ul
            %li
              The cartesian closure restricts from presheaves to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+sheaves"} categories of sheaves
              (e.g.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#MacLaneMoerdijk"} MacLane-Moerdijk, section III.6, p. 136-138
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            with underlying category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(X) = [S^{op}, Set]
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            category of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X)
            for the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+sheaves"} of sheaves
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+structure+on+presheaves"} closed monoidal structure on presheaves
            restricts under the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(X) \hookrightarrow PSh(X)
            to a closed monoidal structure on sheaves.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            a left exact
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} morphism of sites
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in Sh(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in Sh(Y)
            a natural
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_* hom(f^{-1}G, F) \simeq hom(G, f_* F).
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
            operation.
          %h2#references References
          %p The first definition is discussed for instance in section I.6 of
          %ul
            %li#MacLaneMoerdijk
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sheaves+in+Geometry+and+Logic"} Sheaves in Geometry and Logic
          %p The second definition is discussed for instance in section 17.1 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Masaki+Kashiwara"}> Masaki Kashiwara
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Schapira"} Pierre Schapira
              %em
